As a compliment to your story, how about one of the luckiest moments a
character of mine ever had...

The game starts well; Hilda the valkyrie heads down into the Gnomish mines
and picks up the luckstone, gets Mjollnir from Odin, and wishes for some
gauntlets of power.

Hilda heads back upstairs, and begins quaffing from every fountain in sight,
hoping to get another wish. A water demon appears -- no problem, she thinks.
The demon is soon dispatched, but not after he's summoned a couple of his
buddies. So Hilda goes to work on the second demon, and it, too, soon falls
beneath her blows.

Time for the third and last demon. This one has a funny color; must be
something other than a water demon. No problem...

You miss Jubilex. -more-

help...

Jubliex engulfs you.

So, if you were a sixth level valkyrie sitting in Jubliex, who has appeared
on the third dungeon level, what would you do? Panic? That's what I did...

You miss Jubliex. -more-
You feel deathly sick!

Belatedly, Hilda begins to think about escape. After some hunting through
her inventory, sho comes up with a wand of digging. A quick <zap> later, she's
standing outside the demon lord again. Another wave of the wand and she falls
through the floor to safety.

With Hilda's fate sealed, since I had no potions of curing, I decided to take
her as down in the dungeon as possible to maximize the chances of a bones
file being created. The wand of digging ran out of charges on level 12, so
Hilda wandered off to meet her doom...

You die. -more-
But wait! The triangular amulet begins to glow! -more-

I hadn't even realized that I was wearing an amulet...
